.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:23:### S01 - Game outcome rules
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:26:- title: Game outcome rules
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:28:- implementation rationale: The turn loop and terminal-state handling depend on reliable outcome detection before higher-level gameplay state can be implemented.
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:31:- acceptance criteria: All eight win lines are detected; mixed or incomplete boards do not report false winners; full boards return true; boards with empty cells return false; `go test ./...` passes.
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:42:- objective: Add domain-level game state for current player, valid move application, invalid move rejection, and terminal states.
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:43:- implementation rationale: Turn advancement and invalid move behavior are game rules and should not be owned by the command loop.
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:45:- implementation notes: Introduce a small `Game` or equivalent state type around `Board`, current player, and outcome accessors. Start with `X`; alternate only after valid non-terminal moves; reject occupied cells, invalid indexes, invalid marks, and moves after game end without mutating state.
.chr/user/plans/cli-gameplay-plan.md:46:- acceptance criteria: `X` starts; valid moves alternate `X` and `O`; invalid moves preserve board and current player; occupied cells are rejected; wins and draws prevent further mutation; table-driven transition tests pass.
